{"step_index":423,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:39:24Z","content":"Got it! The issue was two-fold:\n\n1. **Over-sanitization**: My previous script version had replaced the notes directly on disk with `[PROTECTED]`, so even with `reveal=true`, the cached file only contained `[PROTECTED]`.\n2. **Missing `Password` field**: The parser was originally discarding KeePass's primary `Password` attribute entirely.\n\n---\n\n### What I Fixed\n\n1. **Restored Raw Notes**:\n   The original note for `mtq-mailsrvp-01` (`root / cy/+v5Zp9IUu)u|jc6Xw,g*`q`) is restored in [inventory/server_pool.json](file:///home/koby/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json).\n2. **KeePass `Password` Attribute Extraction**:\n   Updated [scripts/build_kdbx_pool.py](file:///home/koby/.ansible/scripts/build_kdbx_pool.py) to capture the entry's actual **`Password`** field from KeePass and display it prominently:\n   - Displayed as: `Password : <value>` in search outputs.\n   - Populated as: `ansible_password: <value>` in [inventory/server_pool.yml](file:///home/koby/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.yml) so Ansible can authenticate automatically.\n3. **Security Safeguards**:\n   - Set file permissions to strict **`0600`** (read/write only by user `koby`).\n   - Added `inventory/server_pool.*` to [~/.ansible/.gitignore](file:///home/koby/.ansible/.gitignore) to ensure credentials are never committed.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n\nRun the search again now:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.ansible\nansible-playbook playbooks/kdbx-pool.yml -e \"search=mtq-mailsrvp-01\"\n```\n\n**Output**:\n```text\n=== [Search Results for 'mtq-mailsrvp-01': 1 match(es)] ===\n\n   1. mtq-mailsrvp-01 [SSH]\n      IP(s)    : 172.30.39.153 Port: 30\n      User     : superuser\n      Group    : OMT_PFS.SYSTEME.ALL/MTQ/linux\n      Notes    : root / cy/+v5Zp9IUu)u|jc6Xw,g*`q\n```\n\n*(Or instantaneously via CLI: `./search-servers.sh mtq-mailsrvp-01`)*.\n\n---\n\n### Re-Sync for All Primary Passwords\n\nTo populate the dedicated KeePass **`Password`** field across **all** servers in the database:\n\n```bash\nansible-playbook playbooks/kdbx-pool.yml -e \"action=sync\"\n```\n*(Or `./search-servers.sh --sync`)*. Once synced, each entry will display both its dedicated login password and full notes.","thinking":"**Addressing Over-Sanitization Issue**\n\nThe previous sanitization strategy proved inadequate. Replacing notes containing passwords directly in the data file created an unexpected outcome, where \"reveal=true\" still displayed `[PROTECTED]`. This directly contradicts the expected behavior of revealing the original, not the redacted version. Thus, a better sanitization method is required that prevents this.\n\n\n"}
